  <p class="standfirst">Brands keep asking for the AEO trick. The real problem is usually a clarity problem that AI is exposing.</p>

<section class="tldr" aria-label="Summary">
      <h2>TL;DR</h2>
      <p>Every week another brand asks what the AEO trick is. There isn't one. AI answer engines build shortlists from what they already understand about your brand, and from whether the rest of the web backs up what you claim. Google says so directly: optimizing for generative AI search "is optimizing for the search experience, and thus still SEO," and many popular AEO and GEO hacks "aren't effective" (<a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/ai-optimization-guide">Google Search Central</a>).</p>
      <p>The real work is alignment. What you want to be known for, how you describe yourself, and what AI and the web say about you all have to agree. When they don't, no tactic fixes it.</p>
      <p><strong>You can't hack your way into an AI answer. You have to earn your way in.</strong></p>
    </section>

